---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SOCIALS } from '../consts';
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="Who I am and what I work on."
>
  <div class="shell">
    <header class="page-head">
      <h1>About</h1>
    </header>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        I'm José — a software developer based in Los Angeles. I spend most of my
        time on web applications and AI tooling, which in practice means a lot of
        TypeScript, a lot of reading other people's error messages, and a
        reasonable amount of staring at a terminal wondering why the thing that
        worked yesterday doesn't work today.
      </p>

      <p>
        This site is where I write it down. Not tutorials, mostly — more like
        field notes. The shape of a bug before I understood it, why I picked one
        library over another, what I'd do differently. Writing it out is how I
        find out whether I actually understood the problem.
      </p>

      <h2>What I'm working on</h2>
      <p>
        Replace this with your current projects. A short paragraph each works
        better than a bulleted list of everything you've ever touched — people
        read the first two and skim the rest.
      </p>

      <h2>Get in touch</h2>
      <p>
        Happy to hear from you, especially if you found something here wrong.
      </p>
      <ul>
        {
          SOCIALS.map((social) => (
            <li>
              <a href={social.href} rel="me noopener">
                {social.label}
              </a>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .page-head h1 {
    font-size: var(--step-3);
    margin-block-end: 2rem;
  }
</style>
